    <GaugingStation location="Meagre Farm" name="Kym" number="33012">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound weir gauging a predominantly clay catchment with near-natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Downstream level used to flag non-modularity. Peak flow rating takes non-modularity into account but there is a high degree of scatter. One peak flow ratings applied across period of record. There is a stage offset of +1m in WISKI. This has been applied to all stage data, ratings, gaugings, bankfull and wingwall height.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound weir with triangular profile centre section 3m wide and broad-crested flanks in a trapezoidal channel, 8.5m wide. One of 3 stations used to calculate Offord flow to determine abstraction regime at Grafham Water. No major bridge/weir change from 1959 drawings to H Reed 1994 survey.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Peak flows rejected between 1963 and 1966 due to low confidence. Water year 2002/2003 rejected due to AMAX occurring during missing period in Jan-Mar 2003. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Predominantly natural regime with modest abstractions for agriculture. Some effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly clay catchment - very flashy by Anglian standards. Agricultural, predominantly arable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Rating is not confirmed above QMED/bankfull with any confidence." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
